+
+| Capture before the decision | Counts as the pass | Blocks the `D-n` until | Cleared by |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| valid, live, not conflicted, verdict `a` or `a-with-conditions` | yes, when it is the latest live valid capture | — | — |
+| valid, verdict `not-decidable`, live or stale | no | — (a later round answers it) | — |
+| valid, verdict `b`, live or stale | yes, once cleared, when it is the latest live valid capture | its records exist | one record per objection, `accept` or `reject` |
+| valid, verdict `c`, live or stale | yes, once cleared, when it is the latest live valid capture | its records exist | one `reject` record per objection; accepting a (c) is `run.mjs abandon` |
+| `conflicted`, any validator result, live or stale | by its verdict once cleared, as in the rows above | its records exist | one record per objection and per premise, or `<capture id>:conflict` when it lists none (`reject` there is refused once the `D-n` is decided) |
+| `rejected`, not conflicted, its text has a line `verdict: b` or `verdict: c` | no | its record exists | one record `<capture id>:capture accept\|reject`; either verdict clears the block, `--why` holds the owner's reading |
+| `rejected`, not conflicted, other text | no | — | — |
+| any capture stamped after the `decided` stamp | no | — | — |
+
+| `D-n` status at the exit | Gate result |
+|---|---|
+| `decided` | passes when a capture counts as the pass and no capture before the decision blocks |
+| `superseded` | passes when no capture of the `D-n` blocks |
+| `proposed` | fails, naming the `D-n` |
+| any other status | fails, naming the `D-n` and its status |
 
